// The repos BESIDE the kit `spell` (checked out at `~/www/spell`):  projects of their own that use `spell` as any
// other project would (epic `repo-split` P20).
// - The kit's own folders -- `src/`, then `parser/`, `ui/`, `epic/` and `app/` -- are ONE repo and ONE package now:
//   they're its `package.json`'s `workspaces`, lowest first, not listed here.
// - Each repo here is its own git repo with its own install (spell-brand:  private, never published), at `path` from
//   the kit's folder:  `~/www/spell-brand`, beside `~/www/spell`.
// - `url`:  where `yarn clone <name>` clones it from;  over SSH, falling back to HTTPS (GitHub's login, `gh auth`).
// - Read by `tools/repos.ts` (`yarn clone`, `yarn pull`, `yarn status`, `yarn repos`) and `spell rename imports`;
//   the page server finds a project beside the kit by the checkout's own `page-server.local.json5`, not by this list.
// - This file also marks a folder as a kit (`KIT_MARKER`).
{
  "repos": [{ "name": "spell-brand", "url": "git@github.com:spell-app/spell-brand.git", "path": "../spell-brand" }]
}
